Fix `packages/excalidraw/wysiwyg/textWysiwyg.test.tsx` for these problems, changing only what they need, following the conventions in the shared brief:
1. Senior review blocker (review.json): unit U17 is still not applied; the file is unchanged. Previous attempts failed because a short closing-brace search block (e.g. `  });
});`) matched 6 times. ANCHOR RULE: make exactly two edits, each with a search text that is unique in the file. (1) Imports: search for one existing, unique import line near the top and replace it with itself plus `import { actionChangeStrokeColor, actionChangeHighlightColor } from "../actions/actionProperties";` (actionChangeHighlightColor is now a plain exported Action object, not registered; execute it the way the file executes registered actions, e.g. h.app.actionManager.executeAction(action, "ui", value), or call action.perform via the same manager). (2) The new suite: search for the unique line `      expect(h.elements.filter((el) => !el.isDeleted)).toHaveLength(0);` (it occurs exactly once, inside it("removes a plain text in a single undo")) and replace it with itself followed by `    });
  });

  describe("per-range text styling", () => {` ... the new cases ..., ending so that the file's existing closing `    });
  });
});` still closes correctly (i.e. your replacement must close the old it() and the old describe("history") and open the new describe, and the file's remaining `    });
  });
});` then closes the last new it(), the new describe and the outer describe). Cases (briefs/U17.md): (a) live display while the editor is open: open the editor on an existing text element, set editor.selectionStart=0/selectionEnd=5 (a strict sub-range, not the whole text), apply a stroke colour and a highlight, and assert while h.state.editingTextElement is still set: editor.style.color === "transparent", JSON.parse(editor.dataset.textRanges!) holds the range, and h.app.renderer.getRenderableElements(...).elementsMap.get(id)?.textRanges holds it; (b) live typing shifts/deletes ranges; (c) collapsed selection (selectionStart === selectionEnd set explicitly) recolours the whole element's strokeColor and leaves no textRanges own property; (d) undo/redo: range styling applied while editing is captured EVENTUALLY and folds into the edit session's single history entry, so: apply the highlight to a sub-range, exit the editor (Keyboard.exitTextEditor(editor)), assert textRanges set, Keyboard.undo() -> textRanges undefined / not an own property (or the element reverted per the existing single-entry model), Keyboard.redo() -> restored. No toMatchSnapshot; existing tests unchanged.

The file's current text is under Inputs, marked "current text"; your edits apply to exactly that text.

## Answer
Return ONLY a JSON object {"path": "packages/excalidraw/wysiwyg/textWysiwyg.test.tsx", "edits": [{"search": "<text copied exactly from the current text>", "replace": "<its replacement>"}]} with no other text. Each search must appear exactly once in the current text; the edits apply in order.
If the file does not exist yet, or the change rewrites most of it, return {"path": "packages/excalidraw/wysiwyg/textWysiwyg.test.tsx", "content": "<the complete file>"} instead.
